---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/legal.css';
---

<SiteLayout title="Coven Remote Privacy Policy — OpenCoven" description="How Coven Remote handles saved Macs, passwords, remote screens and clipboard data." canonicalPath="/remote/privacy">
  <section class="site-shell legal-page">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coven Remote</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-lead">Coven Remote connects your iPhone or iPad directly to a Mac you choose. The app has no developer-operated account, server, advertising or analytics service.</p>
      <p class="legal-stamp">Effective November 11, 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="legal-panels">
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Data stays on your devices</h2>
        <p>OpenCoven does not collect remote screens, typed text, clipboard contents, saved Mac addresses, passwords or app usage from Coven Remote. The app does not include tracking or analytics SDKs. Remote screen data and input travel between your device and the Mac you connect to, without an OpenCoven relay.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Saved Macs and passwords</h2>
        <p>Saved connection details and preferences are stored locally. Passwords are stored in the device's Keychain with device-only protection and are available only when the device is unlocked. Deleting a saved Mac also requests deletion of its saved password; any failed deletion is retried on a later launch. Keychain storage can outlive app removal.</p>
        <p>A saved password is sent automatically only after the app checks the chosen address as a Tailscale route. Other connections require explicit approval and credential entry. The app connects to the address it checked.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Screen, text and clipboard</h2>
        <p>Remote screens are displayed on your device. Text recognition runs on the device. Clipboard copying is an explicit action; app-created clipboard items are local-only and expire after two minutes. Pasting to the Mac requires an explicit action, confirms long or multiline text, and does not append a final Return. Interior line breaks use Shift-Return; some Mac apps, including terminals, may execute the text.</p>
        <p>The privacy cover hides the app's contents in the app switcher. Read-only mode suppresses remote keyboard and pointer input.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Network security</h2>
        <p>Coven Remote uses macOS Screen Sharing authentication. The underlying VNC screen and input stream is not encrypted by VNC itself. Use a trusted encrypted network such as Tailscale, and connect only to Macs you control or have permission to access. Tailscale is a separate service governed by its own privacy policy.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Diagnostics and support</h2>
        <p>The app records limited local connection diagnostics and local crash and hang reports rather than passwords, typed text, clipboard contents or screen contents. If you choose to contact support, the message and information you send are handled through that channel to respond to your request. Do not send passwords, private addresses or remote screen contents.</p>
        <p>Apple may process App Store, purchase or diagnostic information under Apple's policies and your device settings. Visiting this support website is covered separately by the <a href="/privacy">OpenCoven website privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Choices and contact</h2>
        <p>You can delete saved Macs, remove saved credentials, change preferences and stop a remote connection in the app. There is no Coven Remote account to delete. For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:hello@opencoven.ai">hello@opencoven.ai</a>. Changes to this policy will be posted here with an updated effective date.</p>
        <p><a href="/remote/support">Coven Remote support</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
